WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.199
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.199 --> 00:00:05.230
Some photos can tell rich, detailed stories.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.350
Other inspire a thousand questions, and cause
the most benign of minds to race with intrigue.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:16.730
Such happened when this photograph went viral
on the internet after it resurfaced in 2011.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:23.430
It’s not a new photograph by any means,
taken in 1935, it has bewildered many an onlooker

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:24.940
for generations.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:31.420
It seemingly depicts a brave, solitary man
refusing to salute Hitler during his speech,

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.719
an act that if noticed at the time, would
surely bring some horrendous punishment upon

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:36.719
him.

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:41.620
People have long asked “who is that man”
and “what or who drives him to risk his

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.210
life in being so defiant”.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.440
I mean it’s evident by the gentleman’s
body language that he didn’t just forget

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.350
to hail Hitler, he’s out to cause some trouble.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:58.850
This badass was German shipyard worker August
Landmesser and August’s brave act of disobedience

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.519
was born out of love.

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:05.410
You had better prepare yourself because we’re
about to embark on a love story that makes

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.860
The Notebook look like a Twilight fan-fiction.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.750
Flash back to 1931.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:16.210
Germany’s economy is in tatters; your family
can’t afford a sauerkraut sandwich between

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:17.210
them.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:21.159
Hitler’s rise to power is just getting going,
handing out leaflets saying “come to our

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:25.659
Nazi rally on Friday night, there’s free
beer all around, and do bring a friend…

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:27.700
as long as they’re German.”

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.760
So what does August do?

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.079
Well he joins the Nazi party of course, in
hope of a better job.

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:39.700
Three years later he met his forbidden love,
a Jewish woman named Irma Eckler.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.340
Just a year later they got engaged.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.189
Because of this August was expelled from the
Nazi party.

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:50.729
The betrothed couple were registered to be
married in Hamburg but a month later the Nuremberg

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:54.729
laws were enacted which made their union illegal.

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:58.180
A few months later they had a baby girl named
Ingrid.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.869
The now famous photo was taken soon after,
when Hitler unveiled a new military vessel

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:05.490
at the shipyard where August worked.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:10.480
His crossed arms and steely gaze directly
into the face of the Fuhrer himself are an

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.460
expression of his anger towards the way his
wife, child and he had been treated by the

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:19.080
political party that he hoped would help him.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:25.330
But I’m afraid this isn’t a love story
with a happy ending, things only got worse

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.940
for August Landmesser and his family.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.990
Irma fell pregnant again and fearing what
would happen to their family, August, Irma

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:38.870
and baby Ingrid attempted to flee to Denmark
but they were apprehended at the border.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.470
August was charged for “dishonoring the
race” and imprisoned for a short time.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:48.040
The Gestapo ordered August to have no further
relations with Irma.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.160
Obviously he refused to follow orders and
only a month later was arrested again and

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.540
sentenced to two years at a concentration
camp.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:02.180
At the same time the Gestapo seized Irma and
sent her to various concentration camps over

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.860
the next few years where their second child
was born.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.340
August would never see Irma again.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:13.750
She eventually met her end in the gas chambers
at Bernburg.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.730
The two children were sent to orphanages and
went into hiding several times until the war

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:19.730
ended.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:25.850
Luckily they survived but our poor protagonist
August Landmesser wasn’t so lucky.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:31.940
When his span in the concentration camp came
to an end, he was drafted into a penal battalion

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.340
and ordered to fight in Croatia against the
allies.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:41.540
These were basically poorly armed and poorly
trained units assembled from German prisoners

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:47.990
of war and forced to fight for the Germans
in what were often suicide missions.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:52.110
August was killed in action in Croatia in
October 1944.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:58.510
But August’s legacy will never die, for
the photograph which captured his bravest

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:04.300
moment will live on for eternity, inspiring
thousands more to fight against seemingly

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.650
unstoppable evils.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.820
If you want to make a difference you have
to be the difference.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.110
Thanks for watching.

